From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uwe Korn <uwe.korn@quantco.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Fix riscv64 runtime call layout without dispatch handle

Node 24.22.1's V8 update changed the riscv64 runtime-call sequence so
that the dispatch handle is pushed conditionally under
V8_JS_LINKAGE_INCLUDES_DISPATCH_HANDLE.  However, it also dropped the
duplicate target-function stack slot that is still required when the
dispatch handle is not part of the JS linkage (i.e. when V8 is built
without the sandbox, which is the conda-forge configuration).

Restore the previous stack layout for that configuration.  Without this,
generated riscv64 code crashes during startup (e.g. `node -h`).

---
 deps/v8/src/codegen/riscv/macro-assembler-riscv.cc | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/deps/v8/src/codegen/riscv/macro-assembler-riscv.cc b/deps/v8/src/codegen/riscv/macro-assembler-riscv.cc
index 0000000000..0000000000 100644
--- a/deps/v8/src/codegen/riscv/macro-assembler-riscv.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/codegen/riscv/macro-assembler-riscv.cc
@@ -200,9 +200,12 @@
     static_assert(kJSDispatchHandleShift > 0);
     AssertSmi(kJavaScriptCallDispatchHandleRegister);
     Push(kJavaScriptCallDispatchHandleRegister);
-#endif
     Push(kJavaScriptCallTargetRegister, kJavaScriptCallNewTargetRegister,
          kJavaScriptCallArgCountRegister);
+#else
+    Push(kJavaScriptCallTargetRegister, kJavaScriptCallNewTargetRegister,
+         kJavaScriptCallArgCountRegister, kJavaScriptCallTargetRegister);
+#endif
 
     CallRuntime(function_id, 1);
     // Use the return value before restoring a0
-- 
